Silo lsteamclient patch 0004 — Steam Input reports the DualSense Silo's Wine offers as an XInput pad

Why: TEKKEN 8 reads buttons through XInput and asks Steam Input only for the controller TYPE, to pick its
button prompts. With Steam Input off for the game (the way Silo's DualSense patches give it the pad over
Bluetooth), Steam reports no controller and the game shows Xbox prompts. With SILO_STEAM_INPUT_DUALSENSE=1 —
Silo sets it when the game's "DualSense as an XInput controller" is on and Steam Input is off for its DualSense —
SteamInput006 reports one controller and only that one: a PS5 controller in gamepad slot 0, where Wine offers the
pad (Silo Wine patch 0024's xinput=pad). Not Steam's own answer, even when it has one: while Steam's overlay is
open Steam takes the pad and reports it. And the game is told neither that the overlay opened or closed
(GameOverlayActivated_t) nor that Steam loaded an input configuration (SteamInputConfigurationLoaded_t, which comes
with the overlay): on those TEKKEN 8 dropped the PlayStation prompts for the rest of the run (measured 2026-11-27 —
hiding the configuration callback alone, or rewriting its handle, was not enough). The overlay still opens; a game
that pauses on it doesn't. Every other call with that handle reaches Steam
unchanged; Steam knows no such handle and answers with its defaults. Without the variable (Steam Input on),
Steam's own answers pass through untouched.

